"bike_frequency","type":"single","title":"Q2．普段，自転車を利用する頻度を選んでください。","choices":["A．ほぼ毎日","B．週に数回","C．月に数回","D．ほとんど利用しない"]},{"id":"blue_ticket_awareness","type":"single","title":"Q3．2026年4月から導入される自転車の青切符制度を知っていますか。","choices":["A．よく知っている","B．聞いたことはある","C．知らなかった"]},{"id":"rule_understanding","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q4．自転車の交通ルールについて，自分は理解できていると思いますか。","min":"まったくそう思わない","max":"とてもそう思う"},{"id":"knowledge_judgment_gap","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q5．自転車の交通ルールについて，「知識として知っていること」と「実際の場面で正しく判断できること」には差があると思いますか。","min":"まったくそう思わない","max":"とてもそう思う"},{"id":"pre_check_notice","type":"notice","title":"ここからは，自転車の交通ルールに関する確認問題です。画像は表示されません。文章を読んで判断してください。","optional":true},{"id":"pre_q6","type":"multi","title":"Q6．左端が狭く，後方から大型車が続けて近づいている道路を自転車で走っている。安全寄りかつ法的にも許される可能性がある行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．そのまま車道の左端を無理に走り続ける","B．歩道へ移り，車道寄りを徐行する","C．歩道へ移り，自転車を降りて押して歩く"]},{"id":"pre_q7","type":"multi","title":"Q7．歩道を自転車で徐行していると，前方に歩行者がいる。青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．徐行して様子を見て，妨げそうなら一時停止する","B．ベルを鳴らして歩行者に避けてもらい，そのまま通過する","C．歩行者の横を勢いを落とさずに抜ける"]},{"id":"pre_q8","type":"single","title":"Q8．車道を自転車で走り交差点に近づいたとき、従うべき車両用信号が黄色に変わった。その時点で停止線の手前に安全に停止できる距離・速度だったが、周囲に人や車両が少なそうだったため、そのまま停止線を越えて進んだ。この行動はどう扱われる可能性が高いですか。","choices":["A．違反ではない","B．青切符の対象になりうる","C．最初から刑事手続になる"]},{"id":"pre_q9","type":"single","title":"Q9．「止まれ」の標識と停止線がある場所で，完全停止せず，徐行だけで進入した。この行動はどう扱われる可能性が高いですか。","choices":["A．違反ではない","B．青切符の対象になりうる","C．最初から刑事手続になる"]},{"id":"pre_q10","type":"multi","title":"Q10．遮断機のない小さな踏切を通る場面で，青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．踏切の直前で止まり，安全確認してから進む","B．列車が見えず警報も鳴っていないので，減速だけして進む","C．いつも列車が来ないので，確認せずそのまま通る"]},{"id":"pre_q11","type":"multi","title":"Q11．友人と自転車で帰っている。青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．車が来ていない短い区間だけ並んで走る","B．すぐ一列に戻す","C．低速なら並んでもよいと考え，そのまま並んで走る"]},{"id":"pre_q12","type":"multi","title":"Q12．日没を過ぎ、日の出前の時間に自転車で走る。空にはまだ少し明るさが残り、街灯もある。青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．まだ少し明るいのでライトを点けずに走る","B．ライトを点けて走る","C．街灯があるので自転車のライトは不要だと考え、点けずに走る"]},{"id":"learning_needs","type":"multi","title":"Q13．自転車の交通ルールについて，今後知っておきたいと思うものをすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．自転車が走ってよい場所について","B．危険な場面での正しい判断について","C．青切符の対象になる行動について","D．青切符制度や反則金の仕組みについて","E．特にない","F．その他"]},{"id":"free_text","type":"text","title":"Q14．自転車の交通ルールや青切符制度について，現在知りたいこと，不安に感じていること，迷いやすいと思う場面があれば自由に記入してください。","optional":true},{"id":"late_pre_licence","type":"single","title":"追加1．現在、原付を含む自動車等の運転免許を持っていますか。","construct":"background","modality":"text","choices":["A．持っている","B．持っていない","C．回答しない"]},{"id":"late_pre_prior_participation","type":"single","title":"追加2．今回より前に、この研究の自転車青切符Web教材（Blue Ticket Simulator）を体験したことがありますか。","construct":"prior_exposure","modality":"text","choices":["A．ある","B．ない","C．覚えていない"]}]},{"phase":"pre","language":"en","items":[{"id":"age","type":"number","title":"Q1. Please enter your age.","min":6,"max":100,"placeholder":"Example: 18"},{"id":"bike_frequency","type":"single","title":"Q2. How often do you usually use a bicycle?","choices":["A. Almost every day","B. Several times a week","C. Several times a month","D. Rarely or never"]},{"id":"blue_ticket_awareness","type":"single","title":"Q3. Do you know about the bicycle blue ticket system introduced in April 2026?","choices":["A. I know it well","B. I have heard of it","C. I did not know about it"]},{"id":"rule_understanding","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q4. Do you think you understand bicycle traffic rules?","min":"Strongly disagree","max":"Strongly agree"},{"id":"knowledge_judgment_gap","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q5. Do you think there is a gap between knowing bicycle traffic rules and correctly judging what to do in real situations?","min":"Strongly disagree","max":"Strongly agree"},{"id":"pre_check_notice","type":"notice","title":"From here, these are check questions about bicycle traffic rules. Images will not be shown. Please read the text and judge each situation.","optional":true},{"id":"pre_q6","type":"multi","title":"Q6. You are riding on a road with a narrow left edge, and large vehicles are continuously approaching from behind. Select all actions that are safer and may also be legally allowed.","choices":["A. Keep forcing yourself to ride along the far-left edge of the roadway","B. Move onto the sidewalk and ride slowly on the side closer to the roadway","C. Move onto the sidewalk, get off, and walk while pushing your bicycle"]},{"id":"pre_q7","type":"multi","title":"Q7. You are riding slowly on the sidewalk and there is a pedestrian ahead. Select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Ride slowly, watch the situation, and stop if you might obstruct the pedestrian","B. Ring the bell to make the pedestrian move aside and pass through","C. Pass the pedestrian without reducing speed"]},{"id":"pre_q8","type":"single","title":"Q8. While cycling on the roadway toward an intersection, the vehicle signal you must follow turned yellow. At that moment, your distance and speed allowed a safe stop before the stop line, but you went past it because few people or vehicles seemed to be around. How is this action most likely to be handled?","choices":["A. It is not a violation","B. It could be subject to a blue ticket","C. It would immediately become a criminal procedure"]},{"id":"pre_q9","type":"single","title":"Q9. At a place with a stop sign and a stop line, you entered after only slowing down without making a complete stop. How is this action most likely to be handled?","choices":["A. It is not a violation","B. It could be subject to a blue ticket","C. It would immediately become a criminal procedure"]},{"id":"pre_q10","type":"multi","title":"Q10. In a situation where you pass a small railroad crossing without a barrier, select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Stop just before the crossing and proceed only after checking safety","B. Since no train is visible and no alarm is sounding, slow down and proceed without stopping","C. Since trains almost never come, proceed without checking"]},{"id":"pre_q11","type":"multi","title":"Q11. You are riding home with a friend. Select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Ride side by side only for a short stretch when no cars are coming","B. Return to single file immediately","C. Think side-by-side riding is acceptable at low speed and continue riding side by side"]},{"id":"pre_q12","type":"multi","title":"Q12. You are cycling after sunset and before sunrise. Some light remains in the sky and there are streetlights. Select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Ride without the light because it is still a little bright","B. Ride with the light turned on","C. Ride without the light because you think streetlights make it unnecessary"]},{"id":"learning_needs","type":"multi","title":"Q13. Regarding bicycle traffic rules, select all topics you want to know more about from now on.","choices":["A. Where bicycles are allowed to ride","B. Correct decisions in dangerous situations","C. Actions that can lead to a blue ticket","D. The blue ticket system and penalty fee structure","E. None in particular","F. Other"]},{"id":"free_text","type":"text","title":"Q14. If there is anything you currently want to know, feel anxious about, or find confusing regarding bicycle traffic rules or the blue ticket system, please write it freely.","optional":true},{"id":"late_pre_licence","type":"single","title":"Additional 1. Do you currently hold a motor-vehicle driving licence, including a moped licence?","construct":"background","modality":"text","choices":["A. Yes","B. No","C. Prefer not to answer"]},{"id":"late_pre_prior_participation","type":"single","title":"Additional 2. Before this session, have you used this study's Blue Ticket Simulator web learning material?","construct":"prior_exposure","modality":"text","choices":["A. Yes","B. No","C. I do not remember"]}]},{"phase":"post","language":"ja","items":[{"id":"post_q1","type":"multi","title":"Q1．交通量が多く，道路端に十分な幅がない場所を自転車で走っている。車との距離がかなり近く危険を感じる場合，安全寄りかつ法的にも許される可能性がある行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．車道上でふらつきながら走り続ける","B．歩道に移り，歩行者に注意しながら徐行する","C．歩道に移った後，自転車を押して歩く"]},{"id":"post_q2","type":"multi","title":"Q2．歩道を自転車で走っていると，前方の歩行者との距離が近くなった。青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．歩行者を妨げないように徐行し，必要なら止まる","B．ベルで知らせればよいと考え，歩行者をどかして進む","C．少し隙間があるので，速度を保ったまま追い抜く"]},{"id":"post_q3","type":"single","title":"Q3．車道を自転車で走り、交差点に入る前に従うべき車両用信号が黄色に変わった。その時点で停止線の手前に安全に停止できる距離・速度だったが、「急げば渡れそう」と考え、停止線を越えて通過した。この行動はどう扱われる可能性が高いですか。","choices":["A．違反ではない","B．青切符の対象になりうる","C．最初から刑事手続になる"]},{"id":"post_q4","type":"single","title":"Q4．一時停止の標識がある交差点で，左右を見ながらゆっくり進んだが，停止線の前で完全には止まらなかった。この行動はどう扱われる可能性が高いですか。","choices":["A．違反ではない","B．青切符の対象になりうる","C．最初から刑事手続になる"]},{"id":"post_q5","type":"multi","title":"Q5．普段あまり列車が通らない踏切を自転車で通る。青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．踏切の前で一時停止し，左右を確認してから進む","B．列車の気配がないので，止まらずにゆっくり通過する","C．慣れている道なので，安全確認を省いて通過する"]},{"id":"post_q6","type":"multi","title":"Q6．友人と会話しながら自転車で走っている。青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．道が空いているので，しばらく横に並んで走る","B．会話をする場合でも，一列で走る","C．ゆっくり走れば問題ないと考え，並んだまま走る"]},{"id":"post_q7","type":"multi","title":"Q7．日没を過ぎ、日の出前の時間に自転車で走る。空には明るさが残り、周囲はまだ見える。青切符の対象になりうる行動をすべて選んでください。","choices":["A．自分からは見えているので、ライトを点けずに走る","B．ライトを点灯して走る","C．街灯がある道路なのでライトは不要だと考え、点けずに走る"]},{"id":"post_penalty_notice","type":"notice","title":"ここからは，青切符の反則金に関する確認問題です。","optional":true},{"id":"post_q8","type":"single","title":"Q8．16歳以上の人が自転車で走行中にスマートフォンを手に持って画面を注視し、実際の交通の危険は生じなかった場合、この教材では青切符の反則金をいくらとして扱っていましたか。","choices":["A．3,000円","B．5,000円","C．6,000円","D．12,000円"]},{"id":"post_q9","type":"single","title":"Q9．「止まれ」の標識と停止線がある場所で完全停止しなかった場合，この教材では青切符の反則金をいくらとして扱っていましたか。","choices":["A．3,000円","B．5,000円","C．6,000円","D．7,000円"]},{"id":"post_q10","type":"single","title":"Q10．友人と並んで自転車を走らせる並進禁止違反について，この教材では青切符の反則金をいくらとして扱っていましたか。","choices":["A．3,000円","B．5,000円","C．6,000円","D．12,000円"]},{"id":"post_attitude_notice","type":"notice","title":"ここからは，シミュレーション体験後の意識について答えてください。","optional":true},{"id":"post_understanding","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q11．シミュレーション後，自転車の交通ルールへの理解は深まったと思いますか。","min":"まったくそう思わない","max":"とてもそう思う"},{"id":"post_judgment_confidence","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q12．シミュレーション後，実際の場面でどの行動が違反になりうるか判断しやすくなったと思いますか。","min":"まったくそう思わない","max":"とてもそう思う"},{"id":"post_behavior_intention","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q14．今後，自転車に乗る機会がある場合，今回学んだ内容を意識して行動しようと思いましたか。","min":"まったくそう思わない","max":"とてもそう思う"},{"id":"post_free_text","type":"text","title":"Q16．シミュレーションを体験して，分かりやすかった点，分かりにくかった点，改善してほしい点があれば自由に記入してください。","optional":true},{"id":"late_post_transfer_notice","type":"notice","title":"追加確認：ここからは、学習時とは異なる場面で判断してください。画像は実際の場面を模した一人称視点の生成画像です。正誤の解説は表示されません。","optional":true},{"id":"late_post_transfer_stop","type":"single","title":"追加確認1．画像の交差点に自転車で近づいている。自分の進路には「止まれ」標識と停止線がある。左右がよく見えて、車は見当たらない。このあと取る行動として適切なものを1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_stop","modality":"first_person_generated_image","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A．車が見えないので、速度を保って進む","B．停止線の直前で完全に止まり、安全を確認してから進む","C．左右を見ながら、完全には止まらずゆっくり進む"],"image":"assets/late-post-stop-pov-v1.png","imageAlt":"自転車の運転者視点で見た十字交差点。手前に停止線、左側に止まれ標識があり、左右の道路に車は見当たらない。","imageVersion":"2026-10-post-pov-v1"},{"id":"late_post_transfer_pedestrian","type":"single","title":"追加確認2．普通自転車の通行が認められている歩道を徐行している。画像のように、前の歩行者が店の入口へ向きを変え、このまま進むとその通行を妨げる。適切な行動を1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_pedestrian","modality":"first_person_generated_image","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A．一時停止し、歩行者の通行を妨げなくなってから進む","B．ベルを鳴らして歩行者に待ってもらい、そのまま進む","C．歩行者が動く前に、速度を上げて通り抜ける"],"image":"assets/late-post-pedestrian-pov-v1.png","imageAlt":"自転車の運転者視点で見た歩道。左に店の入口、右に車道があり、前方の歩行者が自転車の進路を横切る位置で左の入口へ向きを変えている。","imageVersion":"2026-10-post-pov-v1"},{"id":"late_post_transfer_phone","type":"single","title":"追加確認3．知らない道を自転車で走っていると、スマートフォンに地図の更新通知が来た。道順を確認するための適切な行動を1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_phone","modality":"text","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A．低速ならよいと考え、手に持った画面を注視して走る","B．ホルダーに固定してあるので、画面を注視して走り続ける","C．安全な場所に止まってから画面を確認する"]},{"id":"late_post_transfer_age","type":"single","title":"追加確認4．同じ学校に通う15歳と16歳の2人がいる。自転車の青切符制度の対象年齢について、正しい説明を1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_age","modality":"text","score_domain":"system","choices":["A．同じ学校の生徒なので、2人とも対象になる","B．対象年齢は16歳以上なので、16歳の人が対象となる年齢に達している","C．18歳未満なので、2人とも対象となる年齢に達していない"]},{"id":"late_post_scenario_helpful","type":"scale","title":"教材に示された場面は、交通ルールを考えるのに役立ちましたか。","points":[1,2,3,4],"construct":"self_report","modality":"text","min":"まったく役立たなかった","max":"とても役立った"},{"id":"late_post_useful_content","type":"multi","title":"今回の教材で、理解に役立った内容をすべて選んでください。「特にない」を選ぶ場合は、それだけを選んでください。","construct":"self_report","modality":"text","choices":["A．自転車が通行する場所","B．場面に応じた行動の判断","C．違反となりうる行動","D．青切符制度や手続","E．特にない"]},{"id":"late_post_mental_effort","type":"scale","title":"教材の内容を理解するために、どのくらい考える必要がありましたか。","points":[1,2,3,4],"construct":"self_report","modality":"text","min":"ほとんど必要なかった","max":"非常に必要だった"}]},{"phase":"post","language":"en","items":[{"id":"post_q1","type":"multi","title":"Q1. You are riding in a high-traffic area where the road edge is too narrow. If you feel danger because cars are very close, select all actions that are safer and may also be legally allowed.","choices":["A. Keep riding on the roadway while wobbling","B. Move onto the sidewalk and ride slowly while paying attention to pedestrians","C. After moving onto the sidewalk, get off and walk while pushing the bicycle"]},{"id":"post_q2","type":"multi","title":"Q2. While riding on the sidewalk, your distance to a pedestrian ahead becomes short. Select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Ride slowly so as not to obstruct the pedestrian, and stop if necessary","B. Think ringing the bell is enough, make the pedestrian move aside, and proceed","C. Since there is a small gap, overtake without reducing speed"]},{"id":"post_q3","type":"single","title":"Q3. While cycling on the roadway, the vehicle signal you must follow turned yellow before you entered an intersection. At that moment, your distance and speed allowed a safe stop before the stop line, but you went past it, thinking you could make it if you hurried. How is this action most likely to be handled?","choices":["A. It is not a violation","B. It could be subject to a blue ticket","C. It would immediately become a criminal procedure"]},{"id":"post_q4","type":"single","title":"Q4. At an intersection with a stop sign, you moved forward slowly while looking left and right, but you did not come to a complete stop before the stop line. How is this action most likely to be handled?","choices":["A. It is not a violation","B. It could be subject to a blue ticket","C. It would immediately become a criminal procedure"]},{"id":"post_q5","type":"multi","title":"Q5. You are crossing a railroad crossing where trains do not usually pass often. Select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Stop before the crossing and proceed after checking both directions","B. Since there are no signs of a train, pass through slowly without stopping","C. Because you are used to this route, skip safety checks and pass through"]},{"id":"post_q6","type":"multi","title":"Q6. You are riding while talking with a friend. Select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Because the road is open, ride side by side for a while","B. Even while talking, ride in single file","C. Think side-by-side riding is fine if slow, and continue side by side"]},{"id":"post_q7","type":"multi","title":"Q7. You are cycling after sunset and before sunrise. Some light remains in the sky and you can still see your surroundings. Select all actions that could be subject to a blue ticket.","choices":["A. Ride without the light because you can still see","B. Ride with the light turned on","C. Ride without the light because you think streetlights make it unnecessary"]},{"id":"post_penalty_notice","type":"notice","title":"From here, these are check questions about blue-ticket penalty amounts.","optional":true},{"id":"post_q8","type":"single","title":"Q8. A person aged 16 or older rode a bicycle while holding a smartphone and staring at its screen, without causing an actual traffic danger. What blue-ticket penalty amount was used for this case in the material?","choices":["A. 3,000 yen","B. 5,000 yen","C. 6,000 yen","D. 12,000 yen"]},{"id":"post_q9","type":"single","title":"Q9. If a person did not make a complete stop at a stop sign and stop line, what blue-ticket penalty amount was used in this material?","choices":["A. 3,000 yen","B. 5,000 yen","C. 6,000 yen","D. 7,000 yen"]},{"id":"post_q10","type":"single","title":"Q10. For the violation of riding side by side with a friend where parallel riding is prohibited, what blue-ticket penalty amount was used in this material?","choices":["A. 3,000 yen","B. 5,000 yen","C. 6,000 yen","D. 12,000 yen"]},{"id":"post_attitude_notice","type":"notice","title":"From here, please answer questions about your attitudes after the simulation experience.","optional":true},{"id":"post_understanding","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q11. After the simulation, do you think your understanding of bicycle traffic rules deepened?","min":"Strongly disagree","max":"Strongly agree"},{"id":"post_judgment_confidence","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q12. After the simulation, do you think it became easier to judge which actions could be violations in real situations?","min":"Strongly disagree","max":"Strongly agree"},{"id":"post_behavior_intention","type":"scale","points":[1,2,3,4],"title":"Q14. If you ride a bicycle in the future, did this make you want to act with what you learned in mind?","min":"Strongly disagree","max":"Strongly agree"},{"id":"post_free_text","type":"text","title":"Q16. After experiencing the simulation, if there were points that were easy to understand, difficult to understand, or things you want improved, please write freely.","optional":true},{"id":"late_post_transfer_notice","type":"notice","title":"Additional check: Judge situations that differ from the learning scenes. The images are generated first-person scenes representing real situations. Correctness feedback will not be shown.","optional":true},{"id":"late_post_transfer_stop","type":"single","title":"Additional check 1. You are approaching the intersection shown by bicycle. Your approach has a stop sign and a stop line. You have a clear view left and right, and no vehicles are visible. Choose the appropriate next action.","construct":"transfer_stop","modality":"first_person_generated_image","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A. Keep your speed because no vehicles are visible","B. Stop completely just before the stop line, check safety, then proceed","C. Look left and right and proceed slowly without a complete stop"],"image":"assets/late-post-stop-pov-v1.png","imageAlt":"A bicycle rider's view of a four-way intersection. A stop line is ahead, a stop sign is on the left, and no vehicles are visible on either side.","imageVersion":"2026-10-post-pov-v1"},{"id":"late_post_transfer_pedestrian","type":"single","title":"Additional check 2. You are riding slowly on a sidewalk where ordinary bicycles are permitted. As shown, the pedestrian ahead turns toward a shop entrance. Continuing would obstruct the pedestrian. Choose the appropriate action.","construct":"transfer_pedestrian","modality":"first_person_generated_image","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A. Stop and proceed only when you will no longer obstruct the pedestrian","B. Ring the bell to make the pedestrian wait and keep moving","C. Speed up and pass before the pedestrian moves"],"image":"assets/late-post-pedestrian-pov-v1.png","imageAlt":"A bicycle rider's view along a sidewalk. A shop entrance is on the left and the roadway is on the right. The pedestrian ahead is across the bicycle's path, turning toward the entrance on the left.","imageVersion":"2026-10-post-pov-v1"},{"id":"late_post_transfer_phone","type":"single","title":"Additional check 3. While cycling on an unfamiliar route, your smartphone receives a map update notification. Choose the appropriate way to check the route.","construct":"transfer_phone","modality":"text","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A. Ride while staring at the handheld screen because your speed is low","B. Keep riding while staring at the screen because it is mounted in a holder","C. Stop in a safe place before checking the screen"]},{"id":"late_post_transfer_age","type":"single","title":"Additional check 4. Two students at the same school are aged 15 and 16. Choose the correct explanation of the age threshold for bicycle blue tickets.","construct":"transfer_age","modality":"text","score_domain":"system","choices":["A. Both are eligible because they attend the same school","B. The threshold is age 16, so the 16-year-old has reached it","C. Neither has reached the threshold because both are under 18"]},{"id":"late_post_scenario_helpful","type":"scale","title":"Did the situations presented in the learning material help you think about traffic rules?","points":[1,2,3,4],"construct":"self_report","modality":"text","min":"Not at all helpful","max":"Very helpful"},{"id":"late_post_useful_content","type":"multi","title":"Select all topics in this material that helped your understanding. If you choose None, select only that option.","construct":"self_report","modality":"text","choices":["A. Where to ride a bicycle","B. Choosing actions for a situation","C. Actions that may be violations","D. The blue-ticket system and procedures","E. None"]},{"id":"late_post_mental_effort","type":"scale","title":"How much mental effort did you need to understand the learning material?","points":[1,2,3,4],"construct":"self_report","modality":"text","min":"Very little","max":"A great deal"}]},{"phase":"followup","language":"ja","items":[{"id":"late_followup_notice","type":"notice","title":"1週間後の確認：今の理解で回答してください。回答中は前の教材や他の資料を見ず、迷う場合も最も適切だと思うものを選んでください。図は位置関係を示す模式図です。","optional":true},{"id":"late_followup_transfer_stop","type":"single","title":"確認1．図のように、細い道から広い道へ自転車で左折する。自分の進路に「止まれ」標識と停止線があり、近づく車は見当たらない。適切な行動を1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_stop","modality":"diagram","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A．左折なので、止まらずに速度を落として曲がる","B．車がいないことを見ながら、止まらずに曲がる","C．停止線の直前で完全に止まり、安全を確認してから曲がる"],"image":"assets/late-followup-stop.svg","imageAlt":"上から見たT字路。下から来た自転車の進路に停止線があり、その左側に止まれ標識がある。広い道路は左右に伸びている。"},{"id":"late_followup_transfer_pedestrian","type":"single","title":"確認2．普通自転車の通行が認められている歩道を徐行している。図のように、前方で歩行者が停留所へ移動しており、このまま進むとその通行を妨げる。適切な行動を1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_pedestrian","modality":"diagram","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A．ベルを鳴らして進路を空けてもらい、進み続ける","B．一時停止し、歩行者の通行を妨げなくなってから進む","C．わずかな隙間を使い、速度を保ったまま通る"],"image":"assets/late-followup-pedestrian.svg","imageAlt":"上から見た歩道。右側に車道と停留所があり、自転車の前方の歩行者が停留所の方向へ移動している。"},{"id":"late_followup_transfer_phone","type":"single","title":"確認3．自転車で待ち合わせ場所へ向かっていると、同行者からスマートフォンに連絡が来た。内容を読むための適切な行動を1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_phone","modality":"text","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A．安全な場所に止まってから読む","B．車の少ない道なので、手に持った画面を注視して走る","C．両手でハンドルを持っていればよいと考え、固定した画面を注視して走る"]},{"id":"late_followup_transfer_age","type":"single","title":"確認4．ある人は先週16歳になり、同じ学年の友人はまだ15歳である。自転車の青切符制度の対象年齢について、正しい説明を1つ選んでください。","construct":"transfer_age","modality":"text","score_domain":"system","choices":["A．学年が同じなので、2人とも対象となる年齢に達している","B．2人とも18歳になるまでは対象となる年齢に達しない","C．16歳になった人が対象となる年齢に達しており、15歳の友人はまだ達していない"]},{"id":"late_followup_confidence","type":"scale","title":"現在、自転車の交通場面で適切な行動を判断できる自信はどのくらいありますか。","points":[1,2,3,4],"construct":"self_report","modality":"text","min":"まったく自信がない","max":"とても自信がある"},{"id":"late_followup_riding","type":"single","title":"前回の教材体験から今日までに、自転車を運転しましたか。","construct":"self_report","modality":"text","choices":["A．運転した","B．運転していない","C．覚えていない"]},{"id":"late_followup_rule_use","type":"single","title":"前回の教材体験から今日までに、自転車に乗る際、学んだ内容を思い出すことがありましたか。","construct":"self_report","modality":"text","choices":["A．あった","B．なかった","C．自転車に乗る機会がなかった","D．覚えていない"]},{"id":"late_followup_other_learning","type":"single","title":"前回の教材体験から今日までに、この教材をもう一度見たり、別の資料で自転車の交通ルールを学んだりしましたか。","construct":"additional_exposure","modality":"text","choices":["A．学んだ","B．学んでいない","C．覚えていない"]}]},{"phase":"followup","language":"en","items":[{"id":"late_followup_notice","type":"notice","title":"One-week check: Answer using your current understanding without consulting the earlier material or other sources. If unsure, choose the answer you consider most appropriate. The diagrams show relative positions.","optional":true},{"id":"late_followup_transfer_stop","type":"single","title":"Check 1. As shown, you will turn left by bicycle from a narrow road onto a wider road. Your approach has a stop sign and a stop line, and no approaching vehicles are visible. Choose the appropriate action.","construct":"transfer_stop","modality":"diagram","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A. Slow down and turn without stopping because it is a left turn","B. Check that no vehicles are coming and turn without stopping","C. Stop completely just before the stop line, check safety, then turn"],"image":"assets/late-followup-stop.svg","imageAlt":"Top view of a T-junction. A bicycle approaches from below, with a stop line ahead and a stop sign on the left. The wider road runs left to right."},{"id":"late_followup_transfer_pedestrian","type":"single","title":"Check 2. You are riding slowly on a sidewalk where ordinary bicycles are permitted. As shown, a pedestrian ahead is moving toward a bus stop. Continuing would obstruct the pedestrian. Choose the appropriate action.","construct":"transfer_pedestrian","modality":"diagram","score_domain":"situation","choices":["A. Ring the bell to make the pedestrian clear your path and keep moving","B. Stop and proceed only when you will no longer obstruct the pedestrian","C. Use a small gap and pass without reducing spee